---
title: Business Onboarding Format
description: CSV format for onboarding new merchants and their associated payment terminals into the system.
nav:
  path: Partner Services
  order: 1
---

Use this CSV format to onboard new merchants and their associated payment terminals onto Centrapay. An example CSV is provided at the bottom of this page.

## How It Works

Each row in the CSV file represents a single terminal. Rows with the same legal name and merchant name are grouped into one merchant, so a merchant with several terminals has one row per terminal. A single file can contain several merchants and businesses.

Business and merchant details (everything except the terminal columns) must be identical on every row for the same merchant, otherwise the file is rejected.

E-commerce merchants do not have terminals. Use one row per e-commerce merchant, or one row per store URL if the merchant has more than one.

## Field Descriptions

| Field Name | CSV Column | Required | Format/Notes |
|------------|------------|----------|--------------|
| **Business Information** | | | |
| NZBN | `NZBN` | No | 13-digit New Zealand Business Number (optional for sole traders) |
| Legal Name | `COMPANY_NAME` | **Yes** | The legal business name (3-100 characters) |
| Trading Name | `TRADING_NAME` | No | The name the business trades under (3-100 characters if provided) |
| GST Number | `TAX_NUMBER` | No | GST number formatted as 123-456-789 |
| Service Registration Number | `SERVICE_REGISTRATION_NUMBER` | No | Registration number to use instead of an NZBN or GST number, e.g. a Charities Services registration number |
| Contact Name | `PRIMARY_CONTACT_NAME` | **Yes** | Full name of the primary business contact (3-100 characters) |
| Contact Email | `PRIMARY_CONTACT_EMAIL` | **Yes** | Valid email address for the primary contact. The sign-up invitation is sent here |
| Street Address | `BUSINESS_STREET_NUMBER_NAME` | **Yes** | Street number and name of the business address |
| Suburb | `BUSINESS_SUBURB` | No | |
| City | `BUSINESS_TOWN` | **Yes** | City or town name |
| Country | `BUSINESS_COUNTRY` | No | 2 character country code e.g. `NZ` |
| Post Code | `BUSINESS_POSTCODE` | **Yes** | 4-digit New Zealand postal code |
| **Merchant Information** | | | |
| Name | `MERCHANT_NAME` | **Yes** | Name of the merchant location or online store (2-100 characters) |
| Type | `MERCHANT_TYPE` | **Yes** | Either `physical` or `e-commerce` |
| Category Code | `MERCHANT_CATEGORY_CODE` | **Yes** | 4-digit merchant category code (MCC) e.g. `5499` |
| Contact Name | `MERCHANT_CONTACT_NAME` | No | Contact name specific to this merchant (3-100 characters) |
| Email | `MERCHANT_EMAIL` | No | Email address for this merchant |
| Phone | `MERCHANT_CONTACT_NUMBER` | No | Contact phone number (maximum 20 characters) |
| Street Address | `MERCHANT_STREET_NUMBER_NAME` | **Yes** *(Physical)* | Street number and name of the merchant's physical location *(Physical only)* |
| Suburb | `MERCHANT_SUBURB` | No | *(Physical only)* |
| City | `MERCHANT_TOWN` | **Yes** *(Physical)* | City or town name *(Physical only)* |
| Country | `MERCHANT_COUNTRY` | No | 2 character country code e.g. `NZ` *(Physical only)* |
| Post Code | `MERCHANT_POSTCODE` | **Yes** *(Physical)* | 4-digit New Zealand postal code *(Physical only)* |
| Store URL | `MERCHANT_REDIRECT_URL` | **Yes** *(E-commerce)* | The store's website address starting with `https://` or `http://`, e.g. `https://example.co.nz` *(E-commerce only)* |
| **Acceptance Program** | | | |
| Partner Merchant ID | `PARTNER_MERCHANT_ID` | No | Your own identifier for the merchant (maximum 35 characters) |
| Settlement Account | `SETTLEMENT_ACCT` | **Yes** | New Zealand bank account in format 12-1234-1234567-00 where funds are settled |
| Charge Account | `CHARGE_ACCT` | **Yes** *(Payap)* | New Zealand bank account in format 12-1234-1234567-00 used for fees |
| Asset Program ID | `ASSET_PROGRAM_ID` | **Yes** | Asset program identifier `ap_0bhvsTzDEHreYkAGgdKbay` for Payap |
| **Terminals** | | | **One row per terminal** *(Physical only)* |
| Provider | `TERMINAL_PROVIDER` | **Yes** | Terminal provider. One of `Verifone`, `Windcave`, `Smartpay`, `Skyzer`, `Invenco`, `Vista`, `Epay Convenience POS`, `Sektor` or `Eftpos Central Group` |
| Reseller | `TERMINAL_RESELLER` | No | Name of the reseller who provided the terminal. Must match a reseller known to Centrapay |
| Terminal ID | `TERMINAL_ID` | **Yes** | Unique identifier for the terminal (maximum 35 characters) |
| Serial Number | `KIT_ID` | No | Serial number of the physical terminal (maximum 35 characters) |
| Device Model | `KIT_TYPE` | No | Model of the terminal, e.g. `P400` (3-100 characters) |

## Example CSV

The example CSV file demonstrates how to structure your data. It includes:

- **Rows 1-2**: A physical merchant with two Verifone terminals
- **Row 3**: An e-commerce merchant

Notice that the physical merchant rows include a merchant address and terminal details, while the e-commerce merchant includes a store URL instead. Both merchants include a business address.

[Download example CSV](/example-centrapay-onboarding.csv)
